 the value of $2a-b.$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325139 1113 #uuid "1d81ab6b-bf13-5007-90e1-5f3de11a9199" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325139 1145 "From the slope field, we see that the slope is zero whenever $x=-3$ or $y=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/10ae8ed1fe49b32938dba062ad13e39ce1339c6ac9b94d67f679ab60b288be00.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $y=3,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines. \n\nSo, our differential equation must be\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x+3)(y-3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=-3,$ $b=3,$ and $2a-b=2(-3)-3=-9.$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325141 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325142 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325143 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325144 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325145 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325141 13194139534987 true] [17592186325140 1110 #uuid "d89c2edf-2b16-5c3f-9e26-06054752eb7a" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325141 1034 "-9" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325141 1111 #uuid "4aea5516-9024-51d8-ae06-44f4757411ff" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325142 1034 "3" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325142 1111 #uuid "c24690fc-cfcd-5492-a7bc-9384318369df" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325143 1034 "6" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325143 1111 #uuid "17fa48c6-de1f-5d6c-90ea-eac9f19064f2" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325144 1034 "-3" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325144 1111 #uuid "67f4dccb-e141-5cec-be92-14bdc51dfccf" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325145 1034 "-6" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325145 1111 #uuid "7a463d75-1ec4-5c75-8ef1-65cc9c0a1848" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325147 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1089 "q-50143" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/50472b92dc5fbcc8688bb1d5459f910fb2d3f3c0ee564ba671cb6a53ce8df721.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$\n- ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1113 #uuid "e09007b1-58b7-53da-9003-c7cf000369f4" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325146 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/e328914d55b82fdd07147f683aa44aebbc3f3e908f180e6632332119c81ce482.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the line $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\"" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325148 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325149 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325150 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325151 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325152 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325151 13194139534987 true] [17592186325147 1110 #uuid "c7ddd512-d9c5-5c56-b265-e760316dd66d" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325148 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325148 1111 #uuid "e6955f7f-c502-5145-9a31-37d9fb407848" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325149 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325149 1111 #uuid "98674d0b-e981-5b2f-a7b5-2d8de6341cfe" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325150 1034 "I only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325150 1111 #uuid "0647e010-a9c1-53a7-a741-5db6a0f04cee" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325151 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325151 1111 #uuid "ec7a165a-22d1-5a24-9fd5-be65a7b1d524" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325152 1034 "II only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325152 1111 #uuid "8035c635-438e-5b40-8a4b-c504b6bd5df8" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325154 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1089 "q-50187" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/ac08ec40d4aeae745d9aafd2696fc5da7977aa9d01c2766798ac546b829cb112.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1113 #uuid "8b479fc1-a9fe-5521-9397-979fdf022a74" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325153 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/2e9bd658eb426a7e2d5869f2fd9499e846ab82f25edcef6dc5c6f42e38b188bd.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-1$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines. \n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =xy+y=(x+1)y \\\\ {y}^{′} & =(x+1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-1$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>0$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n\n \nOf the remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=xy+y=(x+1)y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=xy+y.$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325155 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325156 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325157 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325158 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325159 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325154 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325155 13194139534987 true] [1759