d:\n\n- First, the slopes become horizontal along the lines $y=\\pm x.$\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {y}^{′}=\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & {y}^{′}={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, for $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes become vertical as $y\\to 0.$ \n\nOf the remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor $x\\ne 0,$ notice that\n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}}$ become vertical as $y\\to 0.$\nBy contrast, \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\to -{x}^{2}\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325162 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325163 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325164 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325165 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325166 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325165 13194139534987 true] [17592186325161 1110 #uuid "ecb4e7c3-58c2-518b-9f13-a0089b40a921" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325162 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{y}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325162 1111 #uuid "7c62a4f3-3c40-546c-a3e4-c2e2537cab7a" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325163 1034 "{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325163 1111 #uuid "8225c449-bbbc-5fb0-99ab-39a1226cbea4" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325164 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{2x}{y}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325164 1111 #uuid "73c44374-dbf3-5791-a31c-6448018eeb91" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325165 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{{y}^{2}}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325165 1111 #uuid "09bae4de-8ce8-5d4a-a6bb-b1833f460385" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325166 1034 "{y}^{′}=xy" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325166 1111 #uuid "f8aa5643-1e40-5829-9d50-92df816e118e" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325168 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1089 "q-50348" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/097a662a461b31dbcadc4e3fc2d9cb5c439c251792b72c768581055783e35379.png)\n\nIdentify the differential equation that generated the slope field above." 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1113 #uuid "bb7cc510-cda6-5038-820e-790968629172" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325167 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/9cee91c4500060ff7b8cb2e35a8748614b9bb7a9b267e2c8ee58d6273a7561f1.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes become horizontal along the lines $y=-x.$\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that satisfy this condition are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\  & {y}^{′}=x+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, for $y\\ne 0,$ the slopes become vertical as $x\\to 0.$ \n\nOf the remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFor $y\\ne 0,$ notice that\n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{x+y}{x}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{x}$ become vertical as $x\\to 0.$\nBy contrast, \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+y\\to y\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{x}.\n$$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325169 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325170 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325171 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325172 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325173 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325170 13194139534987 true] [17592186325168 1110 #uuid "9608b28e-267b-5c91-b8cf-d9bf68620849" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325169 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x-y}{x}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325169 1111 #uuid "e0932323-5bc1-5fdd-890c-1a4e840a0f9c" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325170 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x+y}{x}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325170 1111 #uuid "e3654ca6-5b17-546e-ab38-eaf99d3c034e" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325171 1034 "{y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y}" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325171 1111 #uuid "fc9f0b36-5b23-503c-b219-88f26372aa1d" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325172 1034 "{y}^{′}=x+y" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325172 1111 #uuid "79383d78-369c-504a-9965-dd8156c9e240" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325173 1034 "{y}^{′}=x-y" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534987 true] [17592186325173 1111 #uuid "81458264-689e-5e61-a3fd-1bdae15f7f9a" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325175 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1089 "q-50349" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/6a64064f114ac2e6acafa791c4fda50849cad6f3387c4793bdf991c95ae8e542.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x+y$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1113 #uuid "bb29a817-c88f-55f6-8e13-5c432b07e294" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325174 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/6a119b24c773a25bf3530dbfb8574c710cc37a5e970d92112aee5f489551ef02.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $x=0.$\n\n- For $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $y\\to -1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ and for $x\\ne 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{x}{y+1}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x+y$ does not evaluate to zero on $x=0$ (the value depends on $y$).\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ but for $x\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=|\\frac{x}{y-1}|\\to \\frac{|x|}{2}\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325176 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325177 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325178 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325179 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325180 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325178 13194139534987 true] [17592186325175 1110 #uuid "1079a8c8-1903-584d-927e-27e2e9a1c3c7" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325176 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325176 1111 #uuid "24f19954-91d9-5839-8dfd-4430481d7315" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325177 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325177 1111 #uuid "025ac7b8-4a9e-5c70-9993-e44c5128e455" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325178 1034 "I only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325178 1111 #uuid "cb483467-da99-555e-b04b-2627b9c53591" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325179 1034 "III only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325179 1111 #uuid "0a46a023-3a2f-5832-9f01-1afe62ba4634" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325180 1034 "II only" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534987 true] [17592186325180 1111 #uuid "0d3bb27d-769c-550d-8d71-911fcefe5bc2" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325182 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1089 "q-80714" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/fd7e9afcccbbb635d6bde139697aec0cbaa4bad486ea8b098e96f74bfbefebc9.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2}{y-1}$" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1113 #uuid "30bd4061-472a-5533-b81a-a42df0c3f79b" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325181 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045300/assets/28c4751694caf50f08f73d7ccf3525877e6679901d49854951810f550a65ede2.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope lines on the same horizontal line are all the same. This means that the slope does not vary with $x.$ In other words, ${y}^{′}$ is a function of $y$ only.\n\n- Second, the slopes become vertical as $y\\to 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is a function of $y$ only, but\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to 1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a function of $x$ only.\n\n- Equation III gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2}{y-1}$ is a function of $y$ only, and \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{2}{y-1}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325183 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325184 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325185 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325186 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325187 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1041 "selection" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325185 13194139534987 true] [17592186325182 1110 #uuid "935c9102-fd8f-517d-8075-a759fa9ddcc0" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325183 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534987 true] [17592186325183 1103 #edb/ref 17